2026-10-11T04:34:27.8255452Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8357088Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8366774Z [0m
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8367500Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8368321Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8368719Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8370139Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8371124Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8371494Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8371796Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8372241Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8372442Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8372969Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8373583Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8374088Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8374466Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8374641Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8374891Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8375177Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8375478Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8376108Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8376247Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8376376Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8376547Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8376943Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8377501Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8380144Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8380351Z I will:
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8380611Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8380990Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8381789Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8382497Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8382912Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8383186Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8383468Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8383902Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8384258Z    /root
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8395450Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8396430Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8407689Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8408749Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8409618Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8410205Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8411029Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8428903Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8430265Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8440794Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-11T04:34:27.8441532Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
